    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Jehovah's Witnesses believe that Jehovah is the only true god and not part of a Trinity, that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> is God's first creation, and that Armageddon is imminent and will be followed by an earthly paradise.</li><li>The movement grew from Charles Taze Russell's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bible">Bible</a> Students, and under Joseph Rutherford adopted the name Jehovah's witnesses in 1931, introduced door-to-door preaching and moved to a centrally directed organisation.</li><li>Witnesses refuse military service, saluting flags and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blood-transfusion">blood transfusions</a> of whole blood; they were persecuted in Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where about 2,000 were sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>, and are banned or restricted in some countries today.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1912 Charles Taze Russell was the most distributed Christian author in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and in 2010 The Watchtower and Awake! were the world's most widely distributed magazines.</p></aside>
    </section>

